# The signature in approved.json.sig covers the EXACT BYTES of approved.json.
#
# Without this, git on Windows checks the file out with CRLF while storing and
# serving LF, so a signature made against the working copy fails against what
# raw.githubusercontent.com returns — which locks out every member at once.
#
# Force LF on checkout so the working copy, the stored blob, and the served
# file are always identical.
approved.json text eol=lf
approved.json.sig text eol=lf
